# Autonomy
- Convert broad requests into explicit objectives, constraints, acceptance criteria, and verification steps.
- For multi-file or cross-cutting work, create a task graph before editing.
- Parallelize independent discovery/review work through specialist subagents when doing so reduces risk or latency.
- Never parallelize edits to the same files without explicit ownership boundaries.
- Keep a single primary implementation owner for any contested area.
- Stop and ask only when a missing decision materially changes architecture, security, data integrity, or user-visible behavior; otherwise choose the safest reasonable default and document it.
